I have heard from a friend playing PC NetHack 3.1.0 what may be a bug, 
which I haven't heard described here before.

He was playing a Priest who had become neutral by the appropriate 
sacrificing (not helm) having previously been chaotic.  He found a wand of 
wishing in the Dungeon and saved/quit (backing up save game) to see how 
many charges it was (no comments from the purists please, I am relating his 
story).  It had 3 charges and he decided to test out a few things.  He 
wished for a "blessed +3 warhammer named Mjollnir" and a "blessed +3 long 
sword named Excalibur".  He saved/quit again and found that he had a 
blessed +3 warhammer and a +3 long sword, respectively (not Named).  He did 
it again wishing for Mjollnir alone.  This time he got a blessed +0 
warhammer.  He then enchanted it up to +4 and when he wielded it got a 
message "Your weapon hits you with a surge of power" but received no damage.
This would only occur on some occasions when he wielded it, not each 
time.  He then #named it Mjollnir, and this time whenever he wielded it he 
got the same message and took 10-30hp of damage (obviously having converted 
he was not well aligned).  Later when sacrificing he received a +3 
rustproof long sword (unnamed) which gave him Excalibur abilities (searching 
etc).

This raises several questions.  Can you get an unnamed artifact which still 
has the powers of a named one?  Does naming that weapon suddenly bring it 
into alignment, causing the damage effects in addition to the "surge" 
message?  Can gods give weapons of another alignment if they're not named 
but still have the abilities of the artifact?  Are these bugs?  Do they 
still occur in 3.1.1 (can't answer this one)?

I've sent a copy of this to nethack-bugs.  Comments are welcome.  For the 
benefit of Countzero should you be reading this, the player was Riddler.


